&lt;p&gt;Please join the Columbia Specialized Moot Court Program for our information session on &lt;strong&gt;Wednesday, September 3&amp;nbsp;at 12:10 PM.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt; Food (pizza) will be provided!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All 1Ls will fulfill the First-Year Moot Court requirement by participating in either the Foundation Moot Court Program or one of nine specialized&amp;nbsp;moot court programs.&amp;nbsp; On Wednesday, September 3, student leaders from the specialized moot court teams will present a brief overview of program and the application process. Applications for the specialized programs will open on &lt;strong&gt;Lawnet&lt;/strong&gt; after the presentation.&amp;nbsp; The deadline to apply&amp;nbsp;is Sunday,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;September 14, 2025&amp;nbsp;at 11:59 PM.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More information about the program is available here:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://www.law.columbia.edu/academics/experiential/moot-court/first-year-moot-court" target="_blank"&gt;https://www.law.columbia.edu/academics/experiential/moot-court/first-year-moot-court&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;International dual-degree &lt;/strong&gt;students who are currently enrolled in LPW I may apply for any of the teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2L Transfer Students &lt;/strong&gt;from U.S. law schools&amp;nbsp;may apply for the 3 international moot court teams (Jessup, ELMC and Vis).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

